{"title":"Career roadmap · Planner Assistant","role":"Planner Assistant","summary":"A Planner Assistant supports urban, regional, environmental, rural, infrastructure, transport, and land-use planning teams through spatial analysis, mapping, field surveys, demographic analysis, planning documentation, stakeholder coordination, and data preparation.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"A Planner Assistant supports urban, regional, environmental, rural, infrastructure, transport, and land-use planning teams through spatial analysis, mapping, field surveys, demographic analysis, planning documentation, stakeholder coordination, and data preparation."},{"type":"p","text":"A BA in Geography & Environmental Planning provides a strong foundation in physical and human geography, environmental systems, settlements, population, land use, and spatial thinking. To become highly employable, students should add GIS, remote sensing, statistics, planning methods, CAD, spatial databases, data analytics, and planning regulations awareness."},{"type":"note","label":"Important distinction","text":"Planner Assistant is generally a support/junior role. Professional titles such as Town Planner, Urban Planner, Regional Planner, or statutory planning roles may require a recognised postgraduate planning qualification or specific recruitment eligibility."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Planning Intern, GIS Intern, Planning Assistant"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Junior Planning Assistant, GIS Assistant, Planning Technician"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Planning Analyst, GIS Analyst, Spatial Analyst"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Senior Planning Analyst, Urban/Regional Planning Specialist"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"Planning Manager,